So he's talking about the paddy, the rice. So he plow the land and then he pull in the seedlings, then he transplanted. Mohamed was a rice farmer. But then he faced persecution by the government and had to flee his country. He was registered as a refugee by the UN. And eventually, after undergoing a rigorous background check, he was one of the lucky ones selected for resettlement. I was always thinking how America would be and what I will do there.
所以他在谈论稻田，水稻。他耕地，然后拔秧，再进行移栽。穆罕默德曾是一名稻农。但后来他遭到了政府的迫害，不得不逃离自己的国家。他被联合国登记为难民。最终，在经历了严格的背景调查后，他成为了幸运被选中重新安置的人之一。我一直在想美国会是什么样，我在那里会做什么。

