00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:59.000
One news article from that time reported how company officials met in a war room with maps pinned to the walls. They marked the cities and towns outside their meatpacking plants as potential recruitment zones. They advertised the open positions on the radio, newspapers, and billboards. But not many people wanted to sign up. And so, to dig themselves out of this labor shortage, JBS adopted a new strategy. The company set its sights on a new population. Like the undocumented workers before them, these workers didn't speak much English.
当时的一篇新闻文章报道了公司高管如何在作战室里开会，墙上贴着地图。他们将肉类加工厂外的城镇标记为潜在的招聘区。他们在广播、报纸和广告牌上宣传空缺职位。但没多少人愿意报名。因此，为了摆脱这种劳动力短缺，JBS采取了新策略。公司将目光投向了一个新群体。像之前的无证工人一样，这些工人英语说得不多。

25
