With this influx of refugees, the city of Greeley, was once again transformed. In 2007, just one year after the ice raids, the foreign-born population grew to about 13,000, a 76% increase from seven years earlier. In 2008, Greeley became an official refugee resettlement site. Now instead of moving to Greeley from a nearby city, a person could be brought there directly from a refugee camp, and inevitably, they'd be recruited for a job at JBS. It was a lot for a small city of 90,000. And just like before, it wasn't always pretty. A local mosque was shot at in broad daylight.
随着难民的涌入，格里利市再次发生了转变。2007年，即ICE突袭一年后，外国出生的人口增长到约13,000人，比七年前增加了76%。2008年，格里利成为官方的难民安置点。现在，一个人不再是从附近的城市搬到格里利，而是可以直接从难民营被带到那里，不可避免地，他们会被招募到JBS工作。对于一个9万人的小城市来说，这负担太重了。就像以前一样，情况并不总是美好的。当地的一座清真寺在光天化日之下遭到枪击。

52
00:27:31.000 --> 00:28:09.000
