00:29:48.000 --> 00:30:25.000
and so did his four older brothers when they were first resettled in Greeley. It was and still is the primary job in the area that doesn't require English or any previous experience. I wouldn't say JBS is a long-term job, but for some of the families, they are planning to just do JBS for as long as they can. They have to do it because they have no other options here in the GRILE. And recently, there's been yet another new wave of arrivals, the many thousands of Haitians and Venezuelans who came to the U.S. on temporary protected status.
